431
00:32:11,920 --> 00:32:13,360
It's just part of working somewhere.

432
00:32:13,680 --> 00:32:23,600
But like one thing that really appealed to me with Superwall is like Jake especially, he's built an app and like bootstrapped one on its own that did, like several million in revenue.

433
00:32:24,560 --> 00:32:31,360
And along the way, he needed something like Superwall, which is, if I remember correctly, kind of how the company started at the time.

434
00:32:32,880 --> 00:32:34,560
But, like, those are the things that I wanted to learn.

435
00:32:34,640 --> 00:32:39,680
Because, like, I had had apps for years, but none of them, like, made enough money to where, like, they could just be a job that I had.

436
00:32:40,320 --> 00:32:47,440
And, you know, being able to share with them when I started too, and to say, like, hey, you know, like, I kind of hope this is the last job I have.

437
00:32:47,680 --> 00:32:55,760
To be honest, like, I want to learn from you and do great here, and I want to learn how to grow and make enough money one day to be able to just make software on my own.

438
00:32:56,880 --> 00:32:59,040
And he was like, heck yeah, man, let's do that.

439
00:33:00,400 --> 00:33:05,440
And that's that's the really fun thing is like we see a lot of what works on the App Store and what people do.

440
00:33:06,240 --> 00:33:12,080
And you can pick up those things and apply it to your own work and try and, you know, get into growth mode a little bit more.

441
00:33:12,560 --> 00:33:23,760
And when we talk about the indie stuff, I think that's the big, biggest theme for me this last year or two is I kind of thought a lot less indie and more of just like, how do I make this make money?

442
00:33:24,640 --> 00:33:31,200
You know, like how do I make things grow and become profitable enough for me to take them to that next level?

443
00:33:31,520 --> 00:33:40,560
And you see it all the time at RevenueCat, you see it all the time at Superwall, all these companies that are just, you know., doing insane amounts of money on apps that you would never, ever guess.

444
00:33:41,040 --> 00:33:43,040
And some that you would, some are very obvious.

445
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:52,320
But it's, it's so interesting to look at that data and, you know, kind of learn from it and see the trends and what's working and what not, because it changes all the time.

