00:43:22,960 --> 00:43:23,360
Excuse me.

570
00:43:23,680 --> 00:43:25,200
But they were over different periods of time?

571
00:43:25,680 --> 00:43:27,120
Yeah, I didn't run them at the same time.

572
00:43:27,280 --> 00:43:30,000
So I just did like all organic, no advertising for like two weeks.

573
00:43:30,240 --> 00:43:33,680
Then I just did like, because I don't really have like great tracking in there.

574
00:43:33,920 --> 00:43:36,560
Like I don't even use the Facebook SDK still.

575
00:43:36,880 --> 00:43:39,520
So it's just like I can just kind of see what's going on.

576
00:43:39,760 --> 00:43:41,520
That's where the Apple Search Ads one is better.

577
00:43:41,840 --> 00:43:42,720
Yes, very, very much.

578
00:43:43,040 --> 00:43:45,600
So it's super helpful to kind of look at those things.

579
00:43:46,000 --> 00:44:16,560
Because there you can actually figure out what right because ultimately I think that's what you have to do if you want I mean, if your goal is just to grow your audience or your user base then and you don't care if you're making money or losing money then yeah you can just like pour money into these things but if you want it to be profitable then you kind of need to be able to figure out what is the actual lifetime value I'm getting out of the customers coming from that app right?

580
00:44:16,960 --> 00:44:17,040
Yeah.

581
00:44:17,280 --> 00:44:34,240
And can you only really know LTV after like you've been out on the App Store for a year and kind of seen your churn rate and kind of how people are staying around because I only recently hit that so the like I don't know what was it late October I think is when that one year mark hit for me.

582
00:44:34,560 --> 00:44:45,920
I mean, I'm certainly not an expert at this, but I think the way most people look at this is they'll look at the LTV over a period of like thirty days or ninety days.

583
00:44:48,160 --> 00:44:56,720
And so really what that tells you is like if you have an annual plan, you're like you said it was like fifty dollars a year or whatever, then you get fifty dollars immediately.

584
00:44:56,960 --> 00:44:58,640
It doesn't matter if they turn after that or not.

585
00:44:59,680 --> 00:45:04,320
If you have monthly, I think that's where people maybe look at the 90-day more than 30 days.

586
00:45:05,120 --> 00:45:19,920
But the reason for that is, unless you're like, you have a bunch of capital because you're like VC funded or something, what you really need to know is, am I getting the money back that I put into the machine within this set period of time?

587
00:45:20,160 --> 00:45:22,720
Otherwise, you can't keep putting money in the machine because you run out.

588
00:45:22,880 --> 00:45:22,960
Yeah.

589
00:45:23,680 --> 00:45:23,920
Totally.

590
00:45:24,240 --> 00:45:25,280
Before you even get that back.

591
00:45:25,760 --> 00:45:30,480
And so I think that's what most people are looking at is 30-day or 90-day.

